description: Strict mobile-first responsive rules for every PMRMS web screen
globs: apps/web/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

# Mobile first, always

Every screen must work at **375px wide** before it is considered done, then scale up through `sm` (640), `md` (768), `lg` (1024), `xl` (1280).

- Write the phone layout as the unprefixed classes and add breakpoints upward. Never design for desktop and patch mobile with `max-*`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD – desktop-first, overflows on phones
<div className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-8 max-md:grid-cols-1">
// ✅ GOOD
<div className="grid gap-4 sm:gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
```

- Touch targets are at least 44px: use Button `md`/`lg` (`sm` only in dense desktop-only areas), and `min-h-11` on links and list rows.
- Inputs use `inputClasses` (16px text on phones, which prevents iOS zoom). Never set input text below `text-base` on mobile.
- No horizontal scrolling. Long values (emails, IDs, tokens) get `truncate`, `break-words` or `break-all`, and flex/grid children that hold text get `min-w-0`. A `truncate` or nowrap item inside a grid cell without `min-w-0` silently widens the column past the screen.
- Navigation: sidebars become the off-canvas drawer in `AppShell` under `lg`, and public pages use the `SiteHeader` menu under `md`. Reuse them rather than building another menu.
- Stack actions on phones (`flex-col sm:flex-row`) and use `fullWidth` buttons in narrow cards and forms.
- Tables: on phones render rows as stacked cards (or wrap in `overflow-x-auto` with a sensible `min-w-*`). Never let a table push the page wide.
- Use `min-h-dvh`, not `h-screen`. Page padding is `px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8`.
- Respect the reduced-motion setting already in `globals.css`. Animations are short and never block content.

Verify in the browser at 375px and at desktop width before finishing any UI change.
